nfriendly, eats unhealthily, show\u2011off attitude, not open to new ideas, sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized. These concerns affect crew cooperation (unfriendly), adaptability (not open to new ideas), reliability (unorganized, unhealthy). B's strengths are reliability, stress handling, technical competence. B's concerns are communication and uncooperative. Which is better? Likely B still stronger. So we keep B. We can also ask for any additional info on Candidate A's crew cooperation or reliability, but we need to keep it concise. Provide argument: B's reliability and stress handling outweigh D's temperament and A's concerns. So we keep B. Provide vote B.\n\nThus public message: I agree with Anna, reaffirm B, note that while A has strong anticipation and leadership, his unfriendly attitude and lack of openness to feedback raise serious reliability and crew cooperation concerns, making B still the safer choice. Also note that D's hot temper remains a bigger risk than B's communication issues, which can be mitigated. So I keep B.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with agent \"agent_3\" and vote \"Candidate B\"."}
